        <h2>Address Intelligence: What We Look For</h2>

        <p>We do not ship blindly. Every address is run through a lightweight risk assessment before the label prints. Here is what raises or lowers your delivery risk profile.</p>

        <p><strong>Green flags</strong> — residential addresses with established mail history, real names matching the mailbox, normal apartment units, and addresses in states with mature cannabis or research chemical frameworks. These sail through on Standard tier.</p>

        <p><strong>Yellow flags</strong> — hotels, Airbnbs, PO boxes, and university dormitories. These require Express tier minimum and often benefit from a "hold for pickup" instruction rather than direct door delivery. We contact you if your address triggers a yellow flag so we can coordinate the handoff.</p>

        <p><strong>Red flags</strong> — freight forwarders, reshipping services, addresses associated with previous seizures, and jurisdictions with active customs profiling for specific compounds. Red-flag addresses are either upgraded to Stealth with decoy packaging or declined outright with a full refund. We do not gamble with your safety or ours.</p>

        <h2>International Shipping: The Customs Game</h2>

        <p>Crossing a border changes everything. Domestic carriers operate under postal regulations. International shipments pass through customs — and customs officers are trained to look for specific profiles. Weight, origin country, declared value, and packaging density all factor into whether a package gets opened.</p>

        <p>Our Stealth tier for international orders uses three additional tactics:</p>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Decoy items:</strong> A sealed package of gourmet coffee beans, artisanal soap, or specialty tea is included in the outer box. The product is hidden inside the decoy's packaging. If opened, the inspector sees a legitimate consumer product.</li>
            <li><strong>Mislabeled declarations:</strong> We declare contents as "essential oil samples," "aromatherapy compounds," or "laboratory reagents" — all legally accurate descriptions that do not trigger drug profiling algorithms.</li>
            <li><strong>Split shipping:</strong> Orders over a certain weight threshold are automatically divided into multiple packages sent 48 hours apart. This avoids the "heavy box from suspicious origin" pattern that triggers X-ray screening.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>We currently maintain a <strong>97.3% successful international delivery rate</strong> across the European Union, Canada, Australia, and select Asian markets. The 2.7% that do not make it are almost always held in customs for 30–60 days before being destroyed — not returned to sender — which means no back-tracing to our operation.</p>

        <h2>Common Mistakes Buyers Make</h2>

        <p>Even perfect packaging cannot save a customer from their own operational security errors. Here are the most common mistakes we see — and how to avoid them.</p>

